Semi-automatic atom mapper for two XYZ structures intended for NEB.

Usage:
    python match_xyz.py INT-P-2.xyz INT-P-3.xyz

Dependencies:
    numpy
    scipy

The script:
  * checks atom counts and elemental compositions;
  * aligns the structures using a multi-start principal-axis/Kabsch procedure;
  * assigns atoms only to atoms of the same element;
  * writes the SECOND structure reordered into the atom order of the FIRST;
  * writes a mapping table and reports the aligned RMSD.

IMPORTANT:
This is a geometry-based proposal, not proof of chemical atom identity.
It is most reliable when the structures have similar conformations and
coordinate frames. Inspect the mapping and resulting XYZ chemically before NEB.
Bond-making/breaking and proton transfers can make purely geometric matching
ambiguous. Do not use a high-RMSD or chemically implausible mapping.
